  "question": {
    "text": "The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi></math> amount of thermal energy is developed by a resistor in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> when a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is passed through it. If the current is increased to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, the thermal energy developed by the resistor in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> will be",
