  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Heat energy developed in the resistor due to current is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></math>. Therefore&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;(for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo></math> constant)</p><p>Now required ratio,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>H</mi><msup><mi>H</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#39;</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>H</mi></math></p>",
